         <div type="bio">
            <p>Son of JJ’s daughter-in-law <name type="person" key="joyc94">Helen</name> (née Kastor) by her first marriage to publisher <name type="person" key="flei89">Leon Samuel Fleischman</name>. David Fleischman was born in New York and was educated at Phillips Academy, Andover, Massachusetts from 1934 before studying for a year at Harvard (1940-1), specialising in Literature and History and active in student politics. In 1942 he married <name type="person" key="ID_MISSING">Dorothy Rachel Myers</name>, moved to Newton, Massachusetts, and enlisted in the US Army, serving as a Staff Sergeant in France. He subsequently trained as an accountant in Newton and continued there as a CPA until his death in 1967, aged forty-eight. <hi rend="bold">John Simpson</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
